  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of $n$ terms of the following series $1^{3}+3^{3}+5^{3}+7^{3}+\\ldots$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$n^{2}\\left(2 n^{2}-1\\right)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$n^{3}(n-1)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$n^{3}+8 n+4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 n^{4}+3 n^{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have. $\\mathrm{1}^{3}+3^{3}+5^{3}+7^{3}+\\ldots$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text { Now, } T_{n} &=(2 n-1)^{3} \\\\ &=8 n^{3}-3(2 n)^{2}(1)+3(2 n)\\left(0^{2}-(\\pi)^{3}\\right.\\\\ &=8 n^{3}-12 n^{2}+6 n-1 \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad S_{n}=\\Sigma T_{n}$\r\n$=\\frac{8 n^{2}(n+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{12 n(n+0) 2 n+1}{6}$$+\\frac{6 n(n+1)}{2}-n$\r\n$=2 n^{2}(n+1)^{2}-2 n(n+1)(2 n+1)+3 n(n+1)-n$\r\n$=n\\left[2 n(n+1)^{2}-2(n+1)(2 n+1)+3(n+1)-1\\right]$\r\n$=n\\left[2 n\\left(n^{2}+1+2 n\\right)-2\\left(2 n^{2}+3 n+1\\right)+3n+3-1\\right].$\r\n$=n\\left[2 n^{3}+2 n+4 n^{2}-4 n^{2}-6 n-2+3 n+2\\right]$\r\n$=n\\left[2 n^{3}-n\\right]=n^{2}\\left(2 n^{2}-1\\right).$"
  }
}